1️⃣ User opens UI
Browser
  → http://localhost:8090
  → nginx serves index.html + JS/CSS
✔ No Spring involved
✔ No Gateway involved
✔ Pure static hosting

2️⃣ User clicks Login
Angular App
  → Redirect to Keycloak
  → http://localhost:8095/realms/.../auth
✔ Client: angular-ui
✔ Redirect URI: http://localhost:8090/*

3️⃣ Keycloak Authentication
Keycloak
  → Login success
  → Redirect back to Angular with auth code
Angular exchanges code → gets JWT

4️⃣ Angular calls backend API
Angular
  → GET /api/orders
What actually happens:
Browser
 → Nginx (angular-ui)
 → proxy_pass http://gateway-service:8080/api/orders
 → Gateway validates JWT
 → Gateway routes to orders-service
 → Response flows back
✔ Browser never sees backend ports
✔ Gateway never exposed to public
✔ Perfect security boundary